# pstore.config: the kernel log of a run that ended in a reset or a hang, kept in RAM for the next boot
# (/sys/fs/pstore/console-ramoops-0). For standby forensics on a board without a UART (the HY320, doku/227):
# the region is given on the command line, not in the device tree, so the release tree stays as it is:
#   ramoops.mem_address=0x46000000 ramoops.mem_size=0x100000 ramoops.console_size=0x80000 ramoops.record_size=0x20000
# 0x46000000 lies below the kernel (0x48000000), above U-Boot's console record (0x45000000) and outside every reserved
# region of sun50i-h713.dtsi. Developer fragment: KERNEL_CONFIG=pstore build.sh kernel, never an image.
CONFIG_PSTORE=y
CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM=y
CONFIG_PSTORE_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_PSTORE_PMSG=y
CONFIG_PM_DEBUG=y
CONFIG_PM_SLEEP_DEBUG=y
